# Fixtures are frozen slices of real runs — for a run against a client repo that means
# client file paths, story text and epic names. This repo ships publicly (see CLAUDE.md),
# so the store is untracked by construction rather than by remembering: nothing here is
# ever a candidate for `git add`, and $STABLEMATE_EVAL_FIXTURES moves it off the tree
# entirely when harvesting from a private repo.
.fixtures/

# Eval output: sample-level results, per-sample run dirs (rendered prompts and raw agent
# answers), and the scratch worktrees. Large, and derived — re-run to regenerate.
.evals/

# Benchmark run artifacts and scorecards, per benchmarks/README.md's layout note.
.runs/

# `replay.py` working area: one clone of the fixture app per trial, plus that trial's run
# artifacts and log. Derived and large — the measurement it produces lives in groom's
# telemetry, which is what `replay.py report` reads. Note this is the *working area*;
# `fixtures/*.yml` (no leading dot) is the tracked manifest and stays tracked.
.replay/

# Round output: the zip is written to the paddock work dir, and the pointer beside it is a
# record of a run, not of a baseline. Tracking one is a deliberate promotion —
# `git add -f benchmarks/results/<task>/<label>.toml`, with `url` filled or a note saying
# the zip is capture-machine-local, because a dangling sha256 in a public repo is only
# acceptable when it says so. A smoke or dev label stays untracked and dies with the machine.
results/
